ink:href="eplasty08e7_fig4"/></fig><fig id="F5" position="float"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>Histological sections of control wound (nontransplantation wound: 0.2 &#x000b1; 0.4 pigmented melanocytes) (left) and melanocyte-transplanted wound (transplant wound: 6.0 &#x000b1; 1.4 pigmented melanocytes) (right) harvested at 4 weeks postoperatively.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="eplasty08e7_fig5"/></fig><fig id="F6" position="float"><label>Figure 6</label><caption><p>PKH26-stained follicular melanocytes in the hair bulb as seen under a fluorescent microscope using a Texas red view.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="eplasty08e7_fig6"/></fig><fig id="F7" position="float"><label>Figure 7</label><caption><p>DIC views revealing dark-colored melanocytes (left) and overlapping Texas red and DAPI views (right) of histological specimens from transplanted wounds.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="eplasty08e7_fig7"/></fig></floats-wrap></article>